   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Irregular past",
     "texto": [
      "Many common verbs change form in the past and do not follow the regular endings: **å være → var**, **å gå → gikk**, **å dra → dro**. The form is the same for all persons: **jeg dro**, **vi dro**.",
      "To ask about a finished event, the past is also used: **Hvor var du?**, **Hva gjorde dere?**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Other common verbs",
     "texto": [
      "Learn each pair as a unit: **se → så**, **ta → tok**, **ha → hadde**, **få → fikk**. The Norwegian past is usually translated into English with the simple past: «saw», «took», «had», «got»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
